  "case": "The readers are funders whom board members will meet to talk about the sixth site. They must come away believing that Harborlight's adult learning works and that more adults want it than five sites can serve. The strongest evidence: enrollment rose from 936 to 1,148, and 287 adults were still waiting at year end. Also, 68 percent of learners who stayed at least 12 weeks gained a reading level, and 71 earned a high school equivalency credential. Funders will ask what the new site adds and what it costs. Staff estimate it would serve 180 more learners a year and cut the waitlist in half. The ask is $190,000, the rise from the $1,420,000 FY2026 budget to the proposed $1,610,000 FY2027 budget, which pays for the Eastgate branch library site and two site coordinators.",
